        "id": 234328,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-12-10T20:26:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"deanjday\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/aeb1de/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> deanjday:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>… and make the players aware of that potential up front.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’d recommend making that “… and make sure everyone is okay with that up front.” As we said, the point of the game’s rules is that the players need to be onboard – not just informed. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> This isn’t a game where the GM should be telling the players “yeah, your character is dead”, even if they have a chance to “save” them via challenges&nbsp;– the GM and the players should come up with the story around what happens when the hero is incapacitated.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I mean, for NPCs, go to town! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiley.png?v=12\" title=\":smiley:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiley:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> But for PCs, the player really needs to be on-board for this.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Of course, it’s your game and you can do what you want! :-)&nbsp;But you should know going in that any players who know the game’s rules might take issue with a different approach…&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
